# Build output
#
# One entry per main package, because `go build ./<path>/<name>` drops the binary at the repository
# root by default. A binary not listed here shows up as a large untracked file, and the next
# `git add -A` commits a platform-specific executable into history. That is not hypothetical: a 9 MB
# `vendor_fixtures` and a 4.9 MB `gen_tailwind_collapse` both sat here, and the second one was
# committed before anyone noticed.
#
# The list covers command/ AND the tools/ directories under internal/, which an earlier version did not — it walked only command/,
# so it reported clean while a tools/ binary was staged and waiting. This says which are missing:
#
#	find command internal -name '*.go' -exec grep -l '^package main' {} \; | xargs -n1 dirname |
#	  sort -u | xargs -n1 basename | while read n; do
#	    grep -q "^/$n$" .gitignore || echo "missing: $n"
#	  done
#
# A binary whose name differs from its directory needs its own line: `gen_tailwind_collapse` is built
# from `internal/lint/rules/tailwind/tools/generate_collapse`, so no directory-derived entry ever covered it.
/formatdiff
/gen_tailwind_collapse
/cohere
/cohere-differential
/cohere-dispatch
/cohere-release
/extract_oxc_fixtures
/formatter_comparison
/generate_candidate
/generate_class_order
/generate_collapse
/generate_css_parser
/generate_data_type
/generate_descriptor_base
/generate_descriptor_table
/generate_framework_variants
/generate_shims
/generate_statics
/generate_syntax_tree
/generate_theme
/generate_utility
/generate_value_parser
/generate_variant
/build_dispatcher_package
/vendor_fixtures
/dist/

# Local caches: the graph snapshot and the rebuild cache at the root, and the Swift engine's build
# scratch in swift/.cache, written when the engine checks itself
.cache/

# Operating systems and editors
#
# These are the only entries carried over from the ahra tree's ignore file. The rest of it covers a
# TypeScript application — node_modules, .next, .env, wrangler, a Python venv — and none of that can
# appear in a Go repository, so copying it whole would leave a reader guessing which lines are load
# bearing and which are inherited.
#
# .DS_Store is here because Finder writes one into any directory it displays, and two appeared at
# the root and under internal/ while this repository was being read rather than edited.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.localized
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/

# Stray logs
#
# Nothing here writes a .log on purpose. The entry exists because a long command redirected to a
# file at the repository root is the ordinary way to read output that a pipe would truncate, and
# that file should never reach a commit.
*.log
